+### The B+ branch of the batch
+
+- **Reading history.** Admission first, per transaction: a read version below the B+ boundary
+  marks its transaction too old and counts `PagedTooOldWithinWindow`, before the query batch is
+  formed. So the batch holds only admitted reads, and `hasConflicts` never throws; one too-old
+  transaction cannot keep the others from being checked. Every admitted read, point or range, then
+  goes to one `hasConflicts` call on the single index: sixteen interleaved searches. Every
+  conflicting range is recorded, so a reporting transaction gets all its conflicting ranges.
+  Unlike the paged skip list, ranges of a transaction already known to conflict are not skipped,
+  because conflicts are only known after the batch.
+- **Recording writes.** The combined writes, which come only from accepted transactions, go to
+  one `addWrites` call at the batch version, points as `ConflictKind::Point` and other ranges as
+  `Range`. They are applied one after another. No paths are shared between writes and there is no
+  interleaved insertion.
+- **After the batch.** `cleanup(leafBudget, mergeCandidates, pressure)`, with `pressure` true when
+  the pool's free-page ratio is below the knob.
+
