@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
+# PagePoolTests — test report
+
+Battery: `fdbserver/resolver/PagePoolTests.cpp`. Component under test: `PagePool`, declared in
+`PagedTemporalSkipList.h` and implemented in `PagedTemporalSkipList.cpp`, beside it.
+
+Last run: 2026-09-27, in this tree, whose upstream base is `ef6d39c877`. The report ships
+in the same commit as the code it describes, so it names that base rather than its own
+commit.
+
+## What the component is
+
+`PagePool` reserves one contiguous, page-aligned region up front and hands out fixed
+64 KiB pages from it. A released page keeps its contents; only the first bytes are
+overwritten with the free-list link. The budget (`limitPages`, `heapPages`,
+`indexPages`, `freePages`) is the pool's account of where its capacity currently sits.
+
+`acquire` is what the heap and the index allocator call: it tries `tryAcquire`, runs `gc()`
+if that fails, and tries once more. `gc()` has an empty body for now, so `acquire` behaves
+exactly as `tryAcquire`.
+
+## Tools
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Image | `foundationdb/build:rockylinux9-latest` |
+| Compiler | clang 19.1.5, `-std=c++20 -stdlib=libc++` |
+| Linked against | the fork's `libflow`, for `ASSERT`, `Error`, `TraceEvent` and platform allocation |
+| Build and run | `./run-paged-tests.sh [build-dir] [battery]`, which reads the include flags from the
+real build's `build.ninja` so they cannot drift from it |
+| Coverage | `-fprofile-instr-generate -fcoverage-mapping -fcoverage-mcdc`, then `llvm-profdata merge` and `llvm-cov show/export` |
+
+The battery is a standalone binary, not an `fdbserver` unit test. It has no network,
+no simulator and no trace file, so `INJECT_FAULT` is inert here and a failing `ASSERT`
+terminates the process instead of reporting a case.
+
+## Methodology
+
+- One property per case, named as a sentence about the component.
+- The budget invariant `freePages + heapPages + indexPages == limitPages` is checked
+  after every transition that should move it, not only at the end.
+- Identity of returned pages is asserted, not just their count: distinctness,
+  alignment to `HISTORY_PAGE_BYTES`, consecutiveness of never-used pages, and which
+  page comes back after a release.
+- Mutation checks: the implementation is mutated in a scratch copy and the battery must
+  fail. A battery that has never failed is not evidence.
+- Coverage is measured, classified, and every uncovered branch is accounted for.
+
+## Results
+
+11 cases, 11 passed.
+
+| case | property |
+|---|---|
+| `aPoolStartsEmptyAndAligned` | the budget starts whole and the first page is aligned |
+| `acquiringMovesPagesBetweenCounters` | acquiring and releasing debit and credit the right counter |
+| `pagesAreDistinctAndWithinTheRegion` | every acquisition is distinct; unused pages are consecutive |
+| `anExhaustedPoolReturnsNull` | exhaustion returns `nullptr` for both uses and is reversible |
+| `acquireHandsOutPagesUntilExhausted` | `acquire` hands out distinct pages under each use, returns `nullptr` when exhausted, and hands a released page out again under a new use |
+| `releasedPagesAreReusedBeforeUnusedOnes` | the free list is intrusive and last-in first-out |
+| `aPageReleasedForOneUseServesTheOther` | capacity moves between heap and index use |
+| `reuseKeepsTheContentsBeyondTheLink` | release overwrites only the link |
+| `theWholeRegionIsWritable` | distinct pages do not overlap, first byte to last |
+| `aPoolOfOnePageWorks` | the smallest pool behaves like any other |
+| `aReservationTooLargeThrows` | a region that cannot be reserved throws `platform_error` (1500) |
+
+### Mutation checks
+
+| mutation | detected by |
+|---|---|
+| `release` does not push the page onto the free list | `ASSERT(budget_.freePages == 0)` in `tryAcquire`, process aborted in `anExhaustedPoolReturnsNull` |
+| `tryAcquire` does not advance the unused-page cursor | `acquiringMovesPagesBetweenCounters`; then `ASSERT(index < nextUnusedPage_)` in `release` aborts the process in the same case |
+| `release` clears the whole page instead of writing the link | `reuseKeepsTheContentsBeyondTheLink` |
+| `acquire` returns `nullptr` after `gc()` instead of retrying | not detected, and it cannot be yet: `gc()` frees nothing, so the retry always fails too. It becomes observable when `gc()` has a body |
+
+All four were run against this code and this battery. One is caught only by an assertion,
+which aborts and hides the later cases; two are caught by named cases, one of them before an
+assertion aborts the run; one is equivalent until `gc()` is written. Output is unbuffered and
+each case prints its name first, so an abort shows the case it happened in.
+
+## Coverage
+
+Measured from **this battery alone**, on its own profile. Merging the profiles of the two
+batteries makes `llvm-profdata` report `8 functions have mismatched data`, because each test
+file has its own internal functions with the same names, so these figures avoid the merge
+entirely. The other four components are measured by their own battery and reported there.
+
+- **Lines: 92 across `PagePool`'s ten functions, none missed.**
+- **Every condition component in those functions takes both arms, with no exceptions.** The
+  destructor's `if (base_ != nullptr)` was removed: a constructor that throws leaves no
+  object to destroy, so the guard could never take its false arm. The constructor's
+  failed-reservation arm is exercised by `aReservationTooLargeThrows`, and both arms of the
+  `PageUse` tests in `tryAcquire` and `release` are exercised because this battery uses a
+  page for each use.
+- **MC/DC does not apply**: `PagePool` contains no compound condition. All four of the file's
+  compound decisions are elsewhere.
+
+**What this does not say.** Of the 68 branch arms the compiler counts inside those ten
+functions, 42 are not taken. Those are a separate class, counted apart and not covered: the
+failure arms of the assertions — a violated assertion terminates the process, so it cannot
+appear in a run that reports results — and the body of `INJECT_FAULT`, whose hook is null
+outside the simulator. Two of `PagePool`'s own branches are reached only by
+this battery and not by the other one: the failed reservation, and releasing a page that
+was acquired for index use. That is why the branch percentage is not the figure of
+merit here; the classification is.
+
+## What this battery does not cover
+
+- Violations of the caller's contract: releasing a page twice, releasing with the wrong
+  `PageUse`, or passing a page from another pool. These are preconditions; the
+  assertions present do not promise to detect them.
+- `INJECT_FAULT` on the reservation path. Its hook is null outside the simulator, so the
+  injected failure is unreachable here. The failure path itself is covered instead by
+  asking for a region that cannot be reserved.
+- Concurrency. The pool is not thread-safe and is not exercised from more than one thread.
