+
+### Cleanup budget
+
+The batch budget is `max(MIN_NODES, ceil(inserted × NODES_PER_INSERTED_NODE))`, multiplied once
+by `BOOST_FACTOR` when the pool's free-page ratio is below `LOW_FREE_PAGE_RATIO` or the queue's
+head is at least `LAG_VERSIONS` behind the boundary, and capped at `MAX_NODES`. Each case sets
+the knobs before building the set, with the ratio at 0.5, the minimum at 4 and the boost at 3. It
+steers every tower to height one, so that a pass cleans exactly its budget while enough expired
+cells remain. It sets the insertion counter directly, so the budget is known in advance. Each
+check also requires the pass to have reset the counter.
+
+| case | property |
+|---|---|
+| `theBudgetFollowsInsertionsWithoutABoost` | with no boost, 9 insertions give `ceil(4.5)` = 5; 2 and 0 insertions give the minimum, 4; and a pass never cleans more than the 3 cells that have expired |
+| `scarceFreePagesBoostTheBudget` | 200 short writes leave the eight-page pool at exactly 0.75 free: a knob of 0.76 triples 5 to 15; a knob of exactly 0.75 does not boost, because the test is strict; and the boost applies to the minimum too, 4 to 12 |
+| `aLaggingQueueBoostsTheBudget` | with the head at version 1 and the boundary at 101, a lag knob of 100 boosts, 101 does not; a head newer than the boundary yields no work whatever the lag knob says |
+| `bothConditionsBoostTheBudgetOnce` | scarce pages and a lagging queue together give 15, not 45 |
+| `theBoostedBudgetSaturatesAtTheMaximum` | a boosted 15 is capped at 12, an unboosted 50 at 12, and a cap of exactly 15 leaves 15 |
