+Three mutations first survived and led to changes in the battery, not the code.
+`transferSummary` never marking `maxEnd` for repair went unseen because the removal case used
+ends that sorted with their begins, so every span's largest end came from an old, expired write,
+and an expired endpoint is not a usable bound; ends now grow with the version, so the bound that
+matters is live. A write at exactly the boundary had no case; `aWriteAtTheBoundaryHasExpired` pins
+`<=`. And with insertion cases running before the heap's, a heap mutation aborted inside an
+insertion case before the heap case that names it; the battery now runs bottom up.
