+**Fifteen are caught by named checks. One is caught only by an assertion, and one is not
+detected.** In this section an assertion does not end the run: the reclamation cases run on
+their own thread and record an escaping `internal_error` as a failure of the case, so the cases
+after it still run. That is still detection by assertion, not by a check of the result.
+
+- **Taking the boundary by value** is caught only by the assertion. The search reads a reclaimed
+  key inside `insert`, before a case can look, and no check can see the boundary `insert` used.
+- **Advancing the boundary after `reclaimOldest()`** is invisible in one thread, because
+  `reclaimOldest` does not read the boundary. The order was checked by reading the code instead:
+  in the snapshot, `validationMinRV_ = std::max(validationMinRV_, newestCV.get());` precedes
+  `heap_.reclaimOldest();` in `reclaimForAllocation`, under the comment "Publish the boundary
+  before invalidating references or reusing storage". What the cases do show is that the
+  boundary already covers the page when reclamation returns.
+
+Four mutations first escaped detection, and each led to a change in the battery, not the code:
+
+- **`detach` transferring again was equivalent under the first version of
+  `cleanupAcceptsPreviouslyDetachedTowers`.** The merge takes a maximum, and after one transfer a
+  range target is already marked for repair, so a second transfer into the same predecessor
+  changes nothing. It shows only when the stale predecessor's cell has been recycled and reused
+  by another write before the detached tower leaves the queue. The case now builds that shape,
+  with exact heights and a one-cell budget.
+- **The boundary not advancing, and the guard on the last heap page,** were at first caught only
+  by the assertion on the reclaimed key. Their cases now call `reclaimForAllocation` directly
+  and check the result before any search can run.
+- **`acquire-gc-first`** made two unbounded fill loops in the battery run forever; they now have
+  bounds.
+
+Two cases first failed on the correct code, and the fault was the battery's: a search for a key
+larger than any written does not pass through a tower whose cells all lie behind the path, so it
+detached nothing; and "more expired cells than an index page holds" was stronger than the policy,
+which only needs more than the batch budget.
