+**Eighteen are caught by named checks. Two only by an assertion, and four are equivalent.**
+
+- **The two assertions.** Both mutations read a record that has expired. That changes an answer
+  only when the record's page has been reclaimed, and then the read itself aborts before any
+  answer exists, so an assertion is the only possible detection.
+- **The four equivalents make the search explore more, never less.** Every write reached is then
+  compared exactly, so the answers cannot change: only the cost can, and these cases do not
+  measure it. The last of the four reads the bound through `getKey`, which checks that the page
+  is live and returns nothing otherwise. So it reads no reclaimed memory, and a bound from an
+  expired but readable source still bounds the live ends of its span.
