+
+- **The range search unlinking the towers it explores** was invisible because
+  `expiredNodesStillDelimitLiveSpans` did not build the shape it named. Its filler points were
+  inserted without advancing the mirrored generator, so the "height one" ranges after them came
+  out three cells tall, and the expired tower's span held nothing. The fillers now go through the
+  mirror, and the case checks every level before relying on it. The reclaimed-page part of
+  `unusableSummariesAreExploredNotTrusted` had the same flaw and the same fix.
+- **A range at the read version, and a range touching the read's begin,** were at first caught
+  only by the model run and by cases aimed elsewhere. A write's own level-zero summary is exact,
+  so it discards the span before the record is compared. `rangeOverlapIsHalfOpen` now compares
+  a tower's record at level 1, where a newer write in the span keeps the summary from deciding.
