+## Coverage
+
+Measured from **this battery alone**, on its own profile. Merging the profiles of the two
+batteries makes `llvm-profdata` report mismatched function data, because each test file has
+internal functions with the same names, so the figures below avoid the merge entirely.
+`PagePool`'s functions are measured by its own battery and reported there.
+
+Over the 43 other functions of the file, all but `repairMaxEnd`:
+
+- **Lines: 600, of which 7 are not executed**, all of them in paths classified below.
+- **Branch points in the code as written: 87, with 174 arms, of which 9 are not taken**, all
+  classified below.
+- **MC/DC: 11 compound decisions. Seven are at 100%; two are at 0% and are in `repairMaxEnd`;
+  the other two are partial for reasons classified below.**
+
+| not taken | class | why |
+|---|---|---|
+| `acquirePage`: storage obtained after `gc()` already freed cells (both arms of the inner test, and 5 lines) | unimplemented at the time | `gc()` had an empty body; see the reclamation coverage below for the current state |
+| `unlinkExpiredTower`: climbing to the top of the tower (2 lines) | excluded by invariant | the search meets a tower first at its top: at each level it walks every cell up to the first live one past the key, expired or not, so an expired tower seen lower down was already seen higher up |
+| `unlinkExpiredTower`: a copy that is not linked | excluded by invariant | towers are removed whole, so every copy is linked until its tower goes |
+| `transferSummary`: a source with no `maxCV` (and its MC/DC pair) | excluded by invariant | every linked cell's summary covers at least its own record |
+| `transferSummary`: an empty source `maxEnd` beside a non-empty target | excluded by invariant | a range cell's summary is never empty, for the same reason |
+| `transferSummary`: no repair needed after a target that was empty | reachable, not reached | needs an expired promoted cell that is first on its level, so the target is the prefix, and whose summary names a live endpoint; nothing here builds that shape on purpose and heights are random |
+| `insert`: a tower of full height, `levels < MaxLevels` false (and its MC/DC pair) | reachable with probability 2^-25 per insertion | the height is random and cannot be set from a test |
+
+`repairMaxEnd` is written and called by nothing, so its 52 lines are not executed; it is left out
+of the figures above rather than counted as uncovered.
+
+**What this does not say.** The compiler counts 444 branch arms in those 43 functions. Beside the
+174 of the code as written, 270 lie inside `ASSERT` expansions and 201 of them are not taken:
+they are the assertions' failure arms, which a run that reports results cannot reach, and are
+counted apart. So the claim is that every branch of the code proper is covered in both
+directions except the nine arms classified above, not that every arm the compiler counts is.
+
