+Of the 61 uncovered branch arms, 51 are inside macro expansions, and the only branching macro in
+the file is `ASSERT`: they are its failure arms, which a passing run never takes. The other 10 are
+the source's own branches, below. The function not reached is `occupancy()`, which only
+the Resolver's report printing calls. Every other uncovered arm, by class:
+
+| line | arm | class |
+|---|---|---|
+| 171, 659 | `firstLeaf_` false while `i < visits`, in `reclaim` and `cleanup` | excluded by an invariant: a purge removes at most one leaf per iteration, so the leaves cannot run out before the visits do |
+| 179 | `use == Index && freeNodes_` true after the purge loop | excluded: the loop has already returned on the first free node, and `releaseEmptyPages` removes only nodes of wholly free pages |
+| 182 | the heap is empty when index or heap space runs out | excluded: with no heap page every interval has expired, so the purge has emptied the index and freed its pages first |
+| 414 | the root vanishes in `insertInterval`'s purge | excluded, as the code's comment says: the leaf was reached through a live child, so it keeps a live entry |
+| 492 | `appendRange` returns absent | excluded: reclamation always yields a page while the heap holds one, and a record larger than a page stops at the heap's own `ASSERT` (covered by the pool battery's `aReservationTooLargeThrows`) |
+| 542 | `step` called with depth 0 | excluded: `hasConflicts` steps only live searches |
+| 546 | a node's `maxCV` at or below the read version at the top of `step` | excluded: a child is pushed only when its `maxCV` exceeds the read version; the check is redundant (see the review) |
+| 711, 715 | `levels()` on an expired entry, or on an empty tree | reachable, not exercised: the one call in the battery is on a non-empty tree with no expired entries |
