+## The optimized version (2026-09-29, later)
+
+Everything above was measured on the B+ as integrated, now kept for reference in
+[../initial/](../initial/). The component in the tree has since changed. What each change does
+and what it gains is in `design/beyond-5s/resolver-performance.md`, section 9:
+
+- **`refreshUp`** refreshes the modified node whole and, above it, only the changed child's entry,
+  keeping a count of critical children in each node (`criticalChildren`).
+- **`tryMerge`** refreshes the parent whole, since it loses an entry.
+- **`overwrite`** starts in the first leaf at the last live interval beginning at or before the
+  write, found by binary search.
+- **`addWrites`** keeps one reservation for the batch (`insertRange`).
+- **Queries** no longer prefetch.
+- **A reclaim for a heap page** no longer walks every leaf first.
+
+`verify()` now also checks each node's `criticalChildren` against its children.
+
+**Results on the final tree version:** 22/22 in the ordinary build and 22/22 under ASan/UBSan,
+with nothing reported. Each change was also run alone, as its own variant, against the battery
+before being combined.
+
+Mutations of the new code, on the combined version:
+
+| mutation | detected by |
+|---|---|
+| the critical-children count is not adjusted | checks in 2 cases, asserts in 5 |
+| the changed child's separator is not updated | checks in 10 cases |
+| the parent's maximum is not recomputed (only raised) | checks in 2 cases (the model runs) |
+| `tryMerge` refreshes only the left node upward | **not detected; equivalent**: in an allowed merge neither sibling can be critical. A critical node weighs 15, the merged weight is at most 15, and the other sibling brings at least one entry. So the parent's count changes only through the left node's entry |
+| `overwrite` starts after the possible predecessor | checks in 10 cases |
+| `overwrite` does not restart at the first entry of later leaves | checks in 8 cases |
+| the batch's reservation is not returned | checks in 3 cases |
+
+**Not redone on the final version:** the 35 mutations above and the coverage figures. They
+describe the initial version. The code they cover changed in `refreshUp`, `tryMerge`, `overwrite`,
+`addWrites`, `prepareSearchNode` and `reclaim`.
+
