+## Node reservation sized to demand (2026-10-01)
+
+The patch `btree-paso-02-reserva-exacta` stops refilling a six-node reserve before each write.
+`insertAt` now computes what the insertion needs and reserves exactly that, just before the
+structural change:
+- 0 nodes if nothing splits;
+- 1 for a split below the root, or for the first leaf;
+- 2 for a root split;
+- a range overwrite performs at most two insertions, so at most 3 nodes.
+
+If reserving could have reclaimed the path, `insertAt` relocates. It first discards the pending
+interval if its version is now at or below the boundary. Otherwise it locates the leaf again,
+purges expired entries before comparing any heap reference, and recomputes the demand. Unused
+nodes return at once. v2 remains the default; the pool and reclamation policy are unchanged.
+
+The patch brings three cases:
+- `exactReservationUsesOnlyDemand`: every demand from 0 to 3;
+- `fittingWriteNeedsNoFreeNodes`: a write that fits its leaf takes no node;
+- `pendingSurvivorSurvivesAllocationReclaim`: a reclamation forced between the incoming interval
+  and its live right survivor.
+
+`reclamationDuringReservationSharedPrefix` is new here, as described below.
+
+**Mutations of `insertAt`**, each run against the battery (real FDB libraries, K16/C15):
+
+| mutation | result before the new case | result with it |
+|---|---|---|
+| a root split reserves 1 node instead of 2 | named check in `reclamationDuringReservation`, then the assertion `reservation.size != 0` (26/77) | the same |
+| a split below the root reserves 0 | the assertion `reservation.size != 0` only (28/77) | the same |
+| no relocation after a reservation that reclaimed | named check in `reclamationDuringReservation`: the expired interval was inserted (76/77) | the same |
+| relocation without purging expired entries | **passed 77/77** | caught by the assertion `impl.has_value()`, reading a reclaimed heap reference (77/78) |
+
+The fourth survived because `reclamationDuringReservation` uses keys whose first bytes differ.
+The prefix decides every comparison, and an expired entry left in the destination leaf is never
+read from the heap. `reclamationDuringReservationSharedPrefix` repeats that fixture (seeds 3 and 4,
+one more page) with every key behind a K-byte shared prefix, so every comparison needs the heap.
+It detects the mutation by an assertion, not by a named check.
