+## Reclamation by a common CV list (step 3, 2026-10-01)
+
+The patch `btree-paso-03-cv-comun` replaces leaf-walking reclamation with one intrusive doubly
+linked list. It holds key (heap) pages and individual B+ nodes, ordered by a conservative `maxCV`
+that never decreases:
+- a raised bound moves its node to the tail;
+- split siblings and new roots inherit the source's bound and position.
+
+On exhaustion the allocator advances `validationMinRV` before invalidating anything. It then
+visits the list's head, retiring key pages or removing old subtrees through normal maintenance:
+- a node request may stop at one free node;
+- a key-page request continues until a whole physical page is free.
+
+Pages change use freely between key and index, with no partition and no minimum per use. The heap
+(`PagedTemporalSkipList.{h,cpp}`) joins the list only for the B+ owner, so the paged skip list
+keeps its own ordering. v2 remains the default.
+
+The patch brings three cases, `commonAgeOrderingAndInheritance`,
+`conservativeBoundsAfterRemovingNewest` and `keyRequestReusesNodePage`. It also revises four
+fixtures whose expectations assumed the old policy:
+- `reclamationDuringReservation`;
+- `onePagePoolAdvancesInsteadOfAborting`;
+- `indexReclamationUsesAgeList`;
+- `groupedWritesRestartHintsThroughReclamation`.
+This battery's four own cases (`directSuffixFirstByteDecides`,
+`reclamationDuringReservationSharedPrefix`, `reportAccessors`, `pipelineConfigValidation`) were
+kept unchanged and pass under the new policy.
+
+**Results, 83/83 in eight builds** against the real FDB libraries, with the component and the heap
+of this step and no warning or sanitizer report:
+- K = 16 at C = 15, the default;
+- ASan/UBSan;
+- counters out;
+- C = 23;
+- K = 32 at C = 31;
+- K = 0;
+- inline-only keys;
+- the pipelined path as the default.
+
+The heap is shared, so the pool's and the paged skip list's batteries (`run-paged-tests.sh`) were
+run too: every case passes.
+
+**Real FDB.**
+- The seven integration cases pass with the real build tree's `fdbserver` (v2) and with F's direct
+  path on.
+- The 30 simulations with F on (`sim15-step03`) all pass. The two `CycleTest` runs at 4 pages,
+  which failed before by pool exhaustion, now complete.
+- `skiplisttest` with the model check gives 0 mismatches in 15 runs: 128 pages, 512 pages and the
