+## Permanent key and index shares (step 7, 2026-10-01)
+
+The patch `btree-07-presupuestos-permanentes` ends the free change of use between key and index
+pages.
+- **Ownership.** A pool page belongs to one side from the first time it is taken, and keeps that
+  owner whatever happens later: exhaustion, a workload reversal, or the page becoming empty.
+- **Index pages.** An empty index page stays with the B+, and its nodes stay on the free queue.
+  `releaseEmptyPages()` returns at once for a partitioned pool.
+- **Automatic split** (the default, `MemoryConfig{}`). Each side starts with
+  `max(1, floor(total × 10 / 100))` pages. The rest wait on one unused list: keys take from its
+  front, the index from its back.
+- **Fixed split** (`MemoryConfig{heap, index}`). The two shares are set at once and must sum to the
+  total. The index share must be positive.
+- **Zero key pages.** Allowed only in the inline-only build. A batch with a key outside the inline
+  domain is rejected before anything changes.
+- **Reclamation.** It still follows the common CV list. It now stops when the requesting side has
+  a page (`hasAvailable(use)`), no longer when the pool as a whole has one.
+
+The component patch applied unchanged. Three of its four result files match the patch's hashes;
+`PagedBTreeConflictSet.cpp` differs only by da0a68b567's minimum reuse.
+
+The tests patch applied except for one hunk, which needed hand placement because this battery
+orders its cases differently.
+- **Replaced cases:**
+  - `keyRequestReusesNodePage` becomes `keyRequestCannotTakeNodePage`: a key request no longer
+    takes an empty index page;
+  - `workloadReversalsShareEveryPage` becomes `workloadReversalsKeepPartitions`: no page changes
+    owner across the phases;
+  - `onePagePoolAdvancesInsteadOfAborting` becomes `partitionConfigurationAndExhaustion`;
+  - `indexPagesReturnInAnyOrder` becomes `indexNodesRecycleWithoutPageTransfer`.
+- **Other changes:** fixtures and checks that assumed index pages return to the pool are rewritten
+  in terms of free nodes.
+- **Coverage moved elsewhere.** An automatic one-page pool is now rejected at construction, so the
+  one-page case of advancing instead of aborting is gone. Advancing on exhaustion is still checked:
+  `reclamationDuringReservation` and its shared-prefix variant require discarding batches with
+  `validationMinRV() >= cv`.
