+## Sorted endpoints (step 9, 2026-10-01)
+
+The patch `btree-09-extremos-ordenados` adds a third read engine, chosen by
+`ReadPipelineConfig::sortedEndpoints` (off by default). Neither v2 nor F changes.
+- **Preparation.** One vector holds every query's begin and end, as references, sorted by key; at
+  equal keys ends come before begins, then by query. Each query's `endIndex` points into it.
+- **Traversal.** Depth first, left to right, with one frame per level. Separators and endpoints
+  advance together, and no query is searched on its own.
+- **Open queries.** One shared vector holds the queries crossing the current position. No child
+  gets a copy.
+- **Pruning.** A subtree is skipped when its `maxCV` is at most the oldest read version of the
+  begins in its span and of the open queries. A skipped subtree still consumes its endpoints.
+- **Order of work.** Admission and configuration are checked for the whole batch before any result
+  or `endIndex` changes. Sorting, filling `endIndex` and maintaining the open vector all happen
+  inside `hasConflicts`.
+- **Large batches.** A batch above `UINT32_MAX / 2` queries falls back to the cursor engine.
+
+The component patch applied unchanged on top of step 8. `PagedBTreeConflictSet.h` differs from the
+patch's only by step 8's corrected assertion, and `PagedBTreeConflictSet.cpp` only by
+da0a68b567's minimum reuse. The tests patch applied except for one hunk: it inserts the new
+functions after `internalHeadReclaimsBeforeReservation`, which sits elsewhere in this battery, so
+they were placed by hand. Three cases:
+- `sortedEndpointBoundariesAndCrossings`: three levels, crossing and nested ranges, scrambled input,
+  equality with separators and with virtual point ends, and the pairing of results and endpoints,
+  against the scalar search and both cursor engines;
+- `sortedEndpointAdmissionEmptyAndConservative`: empty tree, batch and ranges, conservative bounds
+  with no live entries, and atomic rejection that also preserves `endIndex`;
+- `sortedEndpointModelUnderPressure`: 180 write batches for each of three seeds on four-page pools,
+  mixed key lengths, points and ranges, reclamation and varying read versions, against the
+  reference model.
+
+**Mutation checks**, each in a scratch copy, battery at K = 16, C = 15. All four were caught as
+reported failures, none only by an assertion or a crash:
+
+| mutation | caught by |
+|---|---|
+| ends after begins at equal keys | both pressure and boundary cases, by the endpoint order check |
+| pruning ignores the open queries' read versions | both, by a wrong decision |
+| an endpoint equal to a record's begin counted inside it | both, by a wrong decision |
+| begins inside a record not checked against its CV | `sortedEndpointModelUnderPressure`, by a wrong decision |
+
+**Results, 90/90 in eight builds** against the real FDB libraries (the same eight), with no warning
+and no sanitizer report.
