+## Node reference prefixes (step 10, 2026-10-01)
+
+The patch `btree-10-prefijo-nodo`, compiled in with `PAGED_BTREE_NODE_PREFIX=1` (default 0). Every
+unit that includes the header must agree.
+- **The reference.** An internal node owns up to 12 reference bytes. It learns them once, as the
+  common prefix of its first two live separators, and never changes them. Split siblings and an
+  internal root's new parent inherit them; a recycled node starts without one.
+- **The separators.** One that shares the reference keeps its next K bytes inline. One that does not
+  keeps its ordinary first K bytes. The internal entry's otherwise unused `end.length` says which.
+- **Where the reference lives.** Leaves keep their neighbour pointers, and internal nodes reuse the
+  same 16 bytes for the reference, so the node size is unchanged: 1,792 bytes at C = 23.
+- **Merges.** Two nodes with different references are merged by re-encoding the moved entries
+  against the destination's reference.
+- **Reads.** Every read path (scalar, v2, cursors, F, staged prefetch, sorted endpoints) understands
+  both forms. Leaves are unchanged.
+
+The component patch applied except for one hunk, in `resolveWriteHint`, where da0a68b567's minimum
+reuse changed the context. Only the leaf neighbour fields were renamed there, by hand, keeping the
+minimum reuse. The header keeps step 8's corrected size assertion. Apart from those two, the
+component equals the patch's. The tests patch applied except for one hunk: the new functions follow
+`sortedEndpointModelUnderPressure`, which sits elsewhere in this battery, so they were placed by hand.
+
+**Mutation checks** (prefix on, K = 16, C = 15):
+
+| mutation | caught by |
+|---|---|
+| a split sibling does not inherit the reference | four cases, by wrong decisions |
+| a merge of different references does not re-encode | `referencePrefixMergeDifferentReferences`, by its encoding check |
+| a compressed separator records offset 0 | four cases, by encoding checks and wrong decisions |
+| the heap comparison skips the first byte past local coverage | **nothing** in the battery |
+
+The fourth showed that no case decided a tie at byte reference + K, the first byte only the heap
+holds. This battery adds `referencePrefixFirstUncoveredByteDecides`:
+- **Keys.** The 12-byte reference and K equal bytes, then a deciding byte.
+- **The check.** For every internal separator, probes one above and one below at that byte must
+  compare accordingly. Point queries are then checked by the scalar search and by all engines.
+- **Against the mutant.** It is caught by the comparison check. No decision changed under the
+  mutant: the misresolved tie is not visible in conflicts in this case.
+
