+## What this battery does not cover
+
+- **Concurrency.** One set, one thread, as the design provides.
+- **The Resolver.** The batch path, admission per transaction, reported ranges and cleanup knobs
+  are covered by the integration cases in `ConflictSet.cpp`; see
+  [ConflictSet.md](../../ConflictSet.md).
+- **Performance.** Nothing here measures time. Counters of the search are compiled in.
+- **Merge policy.** Its thresholds (candidates of 1 to floor(2C/5) entries, results of at most
+  floor(4C/5), the occupancy-trend test) are initial values; the battery checks only that merges keep the
+  invariants and respect the budgets, not that the policy is good.
+- **Leaks.** `detect_leaks=0`: LeakSanitizer is off.
+- **Recovery of a failed insertion.** A pool too small throws `std::bad_alloc` and the set must be
+  destroyed, as settled; nothing tests a continuation after that.
