+## breadthBatch (2026-10-04, experimental)
+
+An optional breadth-first read engine has been added. Nodes are consumed in key order,
+with one open-query list reconstructed per level. Cache-budgeted groups prepare cuts
+ahead of ordered consumption. Heap suffix requests are emitted only after inline ties;
+addresses are reused during a node visit and long suffixes are streamed in windows.
+`breadthBoundaryLevels` defaults to 2. The public selector
+`PAGED_BTREE_BREADTH_BATCH` defaults to 0.
+
+Three cases have been added: `breadthBatchGroupsAndSuffixWindows`,
+`breadthBatchInlineAndAdmission`, and `breadthBatchSuffixAddressReuse`. Shared sorted
+query checks also compare the breadth engine at boundary depths 0, 2 and 3.
+The existing inline-short-key case retains its decision/no-heap checks, with its
+search-activity assertion selected for the public engine.
+
+Standalone validation with FDB stub headers passes 115/115 cases in eight builds,
+including ASan/UBSan, C15/C23/C31, K0/K8/K16/K32, counters disabled, inline-only
+disabled, prefix enabled, and the public breadth selector enabled. This is not
+validation against the actual FDB libraries or deterministic simulation.
+
+Four mutants are detected as named failures: omission of open crossings from the
+child RV bound (four cases); using begin storage for an independent end (two cases);
+removal of prefetch hints (one counter check); and removal of address reuse (one
+counter check). No performance result is claimed.
+
